# Ticket #4471 — Calendar and booking date discrepancies

Ticket #4471 merged 412 unique reports about calendar invites and booking dates not matching. Analysis found three distinct root causes:

## Problems identified

| Cause | Count | Description |
|-------|-------|-------------|
| Parser reads dates month-first; tenants write day-first | 292 | The shared parser assumes MM/DD format but day-first locales write DD/MM. Dates are inverted: 4 July becomes 7 April, 10 March becomes 3 October. Affects most reports. |
| Form hint says MM/DD but tenant types DD/MM | 23 | Booking form shows a MM/DD hint but the tenant's booking-v3 form doesn't enforce it. Users follow their locale's convention instead, creating the same inversion as the parser bug. |
| Other date/booking issues | 97 | Reports that don't fit the primary causes. Mixed in when #4471 was merged; needs separate investigation. |

**Total: 412 unique reports across 3 categories**

## Root cause analysis

Both the parser and form hint issues stem from a failure to respect locale conventions. The parser bug is the dominant cause (292 reports), affecting all channels. The form hint bug is smaller (23 reports) and specific to booking form users. The remaining 97 reports appear to cover other date or booking issues not directly related to the MM/DD vs DD/MM mismatch.

## Next steps

Each problem type has been filed as a separate issue in the GitHub repo so the engineering team can investigate and fix them independently.

